WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.333
Log a service, oil change or repair.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:07.200
Log service. Opens the service form.

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.333
Unit. Pick the truck or machine.

00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:14.200
Date. When it was done. It starts at today.

00:00:14.667 --> 00:00:27.433
Service. Oil & Filter, Tire Rotation, Brakes, Annual Inspection, Repair, Seasonal, Track Replacement or Other. Oil, inspection and tire services reset that item's due date.

00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:34.200
Which track. For a track replacement: Left, Right or Both. It must be filled in for that service.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:44.633
Miles or hours. The odometer for a truck, or the engine hours for a machine, at the service. Opened from a unit, they start at its last reading.

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:53.500
Parts and labor. What the parts and the labor cost. Together they make the cost in the service log and the unit's maintenance cost.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.533
Work performed. What was done, in a few words.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:01:01.200
Performed by. The shop or the mechanic.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:05.233
Next due. Optional: a date for the next one.

00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:09.633
Log service. Saves it and moves the due dates on.

00:01:10.133 --> 00:01:13.867
Close the form. The tour closes it without saving.

00:01:14.367 --> 00:01:20.667
A problem a crew reported. For a problem a crew reported from the phone, use its own button.

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:25.200
Log the fix. Opens the same form for that unit…

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:32.533
The problem is filled in. …with "Fixed:" and the problem already written. Logging it closes the report.

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:36.233
Close it. The tour closes it without saving.

00:01:36.733 --> 00:01:42.333
That's it. You can play this tour in the app any time: press Help, and ask in your own words.
